    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d13">

                <pb facs="0018" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.014 Antarctic/301</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lothian</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 501</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-17">November 17, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the instance of His Majesty’s Government
                    in New Zealand, and under instructions from His Majesty’s Principal Secretary of
                    State for Foreign Affairs, I have the honour to inform you, with reference to
                    the expedition which Admiral Richard E. Byrd is about to lead to the Antarctic,
                    that His Majesty’s Government in New Zealand will be pleased to afford Admiral
                    Byrd’s expedition facilities to establish a base in the Ross Dependency, if this
                    should be desired.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d13-f1"/></p>
                <p>2. I should be grateful if this information could be conveyed to Admiral
                    Byrd.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lothian</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d13-f1" n="3" xml:id="d13-f1-content">
                <p>A similar note, No. 541, dated December 5, relative to the Falkland Islands
                    Dependency, was received from the British Ambassador and acknowledged by the
                    Department on December 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
